{{!--
  dictionary-trick-row.hbs — the generalized trick-row contract.
  View-agnostic: rendered by every migrated browse view for a uniform row
  presentation. Grouping (ADD bucket, family section, etc.) is the view
  template's responsibility; this partial renders one row.

  Two columns, so a reader scanning hundreds of rows can run their eye down
  one edge instead of re-finding each field per row:

  Identity column (.dict-trick-row-identity):
    - trick name, linking to the trick's detail page, the way every other
      entity list on the site links its title. An external-only placeholder
      has no page to open, so its name stays plain text.
    - hashtag (#slug identity): links to the trick's media gallery when the
      trick has media, otherwise a plain token
    - Detail control (opens the detail page, the same destination as the
      name; suppressed for external-only placeholders) and Media control
      (opens the gallery, present only when the trick has media). Both take
      the site's small chip so they read as controls rather than as text.
  Notation column (.dict-trick-row-notation):
    - the trick's difficulty value in parentheses, then the movement notation,
      unlabelled, inside a delimited field so it reads as one object rather
      than as loose words trailing the name. It sits beside the identity as
      reference material and never displaces it.
    - the value rides here, compact, rather than beside the name: only the ADD
      view groups by difficulty, so the other seven views need it on the row,
      but spelling it out per row restates the group heading 24 times in the
      one view that already says it.

  Nicknames ride inline in the identity column, each in quotes so it reads
  distinctly beside the canonical name, never on a line of its own. The
  display-eligible alias set is curated to true community nicknames (names
  players actually use); structural decompositions, initialisms and spelling
  variants are search-only and never reach the row.

  HARD RULES (enforced by this contract):
    - The row states what a trick is, never how far along our own authoring
      of it has got. No status badge, no pending-decomposition note, no
      not-yet-authored marker; those belong on the trick detail page.
    - The difficulty value is the number, not the derivation. The
      operator-by-operator breakdown is detail-page content.
    - Movement notation appears ONLY in the notation column, never as loose
      body text.

  Consumes: DictionaryTrickCard view-model.
--}}
<article class="dict-trick-row{{#if isExternalOnly}} dict-trick-row--external-placeholder{{/if}}"
         data-trick-slug="{{slug}}"
         data-media-coverage="{{mediaCoverage}}">
  <div class="dict-trick-row-identity">
    {{#if isExternalOnly}}
      <span class="dict-trick-row-title">{{displayName}}</span>
    {{else}}
      <a class="dict-trick-row-title" href="{{href}}">{{displayName}}</a>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if commonAliases.length}}
      <span class="dict-trick-row-nicknames" aria-label="Also called">{{#each commonAliases}}&ldquo;{{this}}&rdquo;{{#unless @last}} {{/unless}}{{/each}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if hashtagHref}}
      <a class="hashtag hashtag--media" href="{{hashtagHref}}" aria-label="Media for this trick">{{hashtag}}</a>
    {{else}}
      <span class="hashtag" aria-label="Tag identity">{{hashtag}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    {{#unless isExternalOnly}}
      <a class="tag-chip tag-chip--sm" href="{{href}}">Detail</a>
    {{/unless}}
    {{#if hashtagHref}}
      <a class="tag-chip tag-chip--sm" href="{{hashtagHref}}">Media</a>
    {{/if}}

  </div>

  <div class="dict-trick-row-notation">
    <span class="dict-trick-row-add" aria-label="Difficulty value">{{#if adds}}({{adds}}){{else}}(?){{/if}}</span>
    {{#if operationalNotation}}
      <code class="dict-trick-row-notation-value">{{#each operationalNotation.tokens}}<span class="op-token op-token--{{cssRole}}" data-role="{{role}}" title="{{label}}">{{text}}</span>{{#unless @last}} {{/unless}}{{/each}}</code>
    {{else if firstClassChainValue}}
      {{!-- First-class atoms/tricks suppress operationalNotation; their chain
           rides firstClassChainValue (a plain curator string). --}}
      <code class="dict-trick-row-notation-value">{{firstClassChainValue}}</code>
    {{/if}}
  </div>

  {{#if placeholderNote}}
  <p class="dict-trick-row-placeholder-note">{{placeholderNote}}</p>
  {{/if}}
</article>
